= Death of Plekahnov

Georgi Plekahnov, nicknamed the "Father of Russian Marxism", has died of tuberculosis at the age of 61. 

A founding leader of the country's first revolutionary Marxist organization, Plekhanov laid the groundwork for the Communist Party we have today, helping shape Lenin's own theoretical development along the way.  

Though for the past several months, he had been a vehement and outspoken opponent of the Bolsheviks and the October Revolution, at the head of a small circle of followers known as the "Unity" group (which generally leaned even further right than the Menshevik Defencists). 

Nonetheless, Plekhanov is still hailed as an important Marxist theoretician and leader, even among the Bolsheviks. For all their differences, it seems Lenin cannot help but mourn his old mentor, ally, and friend. 
